From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:19:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 648/648] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: invert the
 touchscreen's axes

The controller's raw axes run opposite to the panel's on both sides.
Describe that with touchscreen-inverted-x and touchscreen-inverted-y, now
that the driver no longer turns contacts to the vendor's landscape layout,
so touch reports the panel's portrait coordinates, 1080x2160.

The inversion comes from a calibration matrix that tracked the finger with
the old driver's mapping; it has not been tested with this change.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 934f242..675e371 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -356,6 +356,8 @@
 		pinctrl-0 = <&touchscreen_pins>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
 		interrupts = <8 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		touchscreen-inverted-x;
+		touchscreen-inverted-y;
 	};
 };
 
